      "raw_response": "ANSWER: SUPPORTED. The abstract suggests that YAP/TAZ activation is involved in the process of intestinal regeneration, especially in a mouse model of ulcerative colitis, as it describes the induction of a primitive cell fate through extracellular matrix remodeling and increased FAK/Src signaling, which are linked to YAP/TAZ activation. The study also shows that a collagen 3D matrix supplemented with Wnt ligands can sustain YAP/TAZ activity and induce cell fate conversion, implicating cellular reprogramming as essential for tissue regeneration.\n\nSource: B.L. Rao et al., \"YAP/TAZ-Dependent Reprogramming of Colonic Epithelium Links ECM Remodeling to Tissue Regeneration,\" Nature Communications, vol. 11, no. 1, 2020, doi: 10.1038/s41477-020-00866-8. (Source provides strong support for the claim)",
